{"name":"Harajuku Girl","hex":"#504a6f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"girl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female child.","A woman, especially a young and often attractive woman."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feminize or girlify; to gender as a girl or as for girls.","To staff with or as a girl or girls."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/girl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Harajuku Girls","blocks":[{"text":"The Harajuku Girls are four Japanese and Japanese-American backup dancers featured in stage shows and music videos for Gwen Stefani during her solo pop/dance-record career. The women also act as an entourage at Stefani's public appearances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/HarajukuGirls.jpg/330px-HarajukuGirls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harajuku_Girls","wikidata":"Q2290368"},{"title":"Harajuku","blocks":[{"text":"Harajuku  is a district in Shibuya, Tokyo. Harajuku is the common name given to a geographic area spreading from Harajuku Station to Omotesando, corresponding on official maps of Shibuya ward as Jingūmae 1 chōme to 4 chōme. In popular reference, Harajuku also encompasses many smaller backstreets such as Takeshita Street and Cat Street spreading from Sendagaya in the north to Shibuya in the south."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/JRE-Harajuku-Station-07.jpg/330px-JRE-Harajuku-Station-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harajuku","wikidata":"Q746573"},{"title":"Girl","blocks":[{"text":"A girl is a young female human, usually a child or an adolescent. While the term girl has other meanings, including young woman, daughter, or girlfriend regardless of age, the first meaning is the most common one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg/330px-Young_girl_smiling_in_sunshine_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl","wikidata":"Q3031"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/MayaChino.jpg/500px-MayaChino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/MayaChino.jpg/500px-MayaChino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maya Chino (\"Love\") during a stage performance of Harajuku Girls","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMayaChino.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Omote-sando03s3200.jpg/500px-Omote-sando03s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Omote-sando03s3200.jpg/1280px-Omote-sando03s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Omote-sando03s3200.jpg/500px-Omote-sando03s3200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Omotesando Hills, Jingumae","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOmote-sando03s3200.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg/500px-Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg/1280px-Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg/500px-Cat_Street%2C_Ura_Harajuku_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb